    <IRS990ScheduleO documentId="990O" softwareId="24019898" softwareVersionNum="24.0.1.0">
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part III, Line 4a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Our Family Workshop is a court approved co-parenting program for the whole family. Children learn how to share their thoughts and feelings about their family situations, that they are not alone and that their parents divorce is not their fault, thus freeing them up from self-blame. Parents gain insight into their words, actions and behaviors and learn how to accept the thoughts and feelings of their children without judging, minimizing or invalidating them. This program was offered virtually in 2024. During the program, children prepare posters for graduation. The six and seven year olds creasted a graduation poster that read, Things we learned in the Family Workshop I learned that you are not the reason why your parents divorce, both parents love me, its ok to live in two homes and I learned about feelings. Children who attend this program find their voice and learn ways to share their thoughts and feelings in constructive and creative ways. Whether in-person or virtual, Kids Turn San Diego continues to change lives by empowering children and healing families.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part III, Line 4b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The Cooperative Co-Parenting Program is a high conflict court approved co-parenting class. This program is offered virtually and helps parents learn about emotional and thought triggers, what they are, where they came from and ways to avoid them. Parents gain new awareness of their own thoughts and behaviors and learn co-parenting skills that will help them avoid emotional and thought triggers, and which help to shift their attitude and behavior toward the other parent. Parents also learn that through loss, anger and pain, positive changes are possible, no matter how desperate they may feel.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part III, Line 4c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Our Counseling Program offers a continuum of care for children and parents who have attended our co-parenting programs. For children, we provide a safe place for children ages 5-17 to talk about their family situation and to further develop coping and communication skills that help them manage themselves within their two homes. For parents, as way to gain individual support and further skill building, we offer advanced refresher Continue the Conversation Classes and The Graduate Program. These services are primarily offered virtually. Kids Turn San Diego is thankful to our funders who provided grants and donations for us to provide counseling services at no cost to the family. Support for our adult programs is provided through grant funding.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 11b</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Executive Director reviews the 990 tax return contents and disclosures with CPA prior to filing. Executive Director then presents the 990 to the Finance Committee for review. The Finance Committee presents the reviewed 990 to the Board of Directors for final approval prior to filing.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 12c</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Annual evaluation of conflict of interest statements are performed by the Board of Directors.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section B, Line 15a</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The executive team of the Board of Directors researches Executive Director salaries via a salary assessor and head hunters. The Executive Director researches program director salaries by reviewing job postings of other Non-Profit Organizations in San Diego and Orange Counties.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 18</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>990 is available for review at www.guidestar.org and www.charitynavigator.org</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part VI, Section C, Line 19</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Documents are available upon request via mail or email.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Form 990, Part XII, Line 1</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>The Organization uses the modified cash basis of accounting. Modifications to the cash basis include recording deferred revenue for unearned program service fees and employees accrued vacation.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleO>
